// Entra ID sign-in ingestion into the WORKSPACE.
//
// CORRECTED 2026-07-26. This file previously said SigninLogs and EntraIdSignInEvents
// were the same data under two surface-specific names. They are not. They have
// different PRODUCERS:
//   SigninLogs           - Log Analytics workspace; written by the Entra diagnostic
//                          setting; scoped by the log types you selected; BILLABLE.
//   EntraIdSignInEvents  - Defender XDR lake; written by XDR regardless of your
//                          connector; every sign-in class; FREE.
// On the unified Defender surface both resolve in one query with very different
// counts (6 vs 972 on 2026-07-26). Only the first tells you your connector works.
//
// An empty SigninLogs shortly after Apply is propagation lag (~10-15 min), not a
// naming mismatch and not a licensing failure. Sign-in ingestion requires Entra
// P1/P2 (confirmed live via the E5 trial).
SigninLogs
| where TimeGenerated > ago(1h)
| project TimeGenerated, UserPrincipalName, ResultType, AppDisplayName, IPAddress, Location
| order by TimeGenerated desc
